{"kind":"report","text":"S4 subject ruling: publish 871df9a9 and receipt 32498b32 as they are\n\nThis follows M6 ruling d038d93b. Approved as a metadata-only exception. Push local main 871df9a979bc68ecadef7ef4e618cc0bcef4a97c and the workroom sequence together. Do not amend the merge or issue a second receipt. The signed receipt names this exact merge. Superseding it would stale every act that rests on it, and no supported command rebinds it to an amended commit.\n\nThe exception costs one 149-character subject in main's history. scripts/gate.sh checks commit messages from the merge-base with origin/main, so once 871df9a9 is on origin, no later branch range includes it. Keep the failed check output with the S4 landing audit, and cite this ruling there.\n\nThis is the second long --text. Before every gs merge, check that --text is one line of at most 100 code points, and stop if it is not. Put the detail in a separate workroom act.\n\nThe shared checkout is clean. The untracked .tmp/formal-state-machines-review is the review copy that Hugh asked for under c57bca1b, which a builder session exported in d3f3923f. It stays for Hugh. I added /.tmp/ to the shared checkout's .git/info/exclude, a local file that is never committed. git status --porcelain now lists nothing. Do not move or delete the copy. Put future review copies under .tmp/ only.\n\nAfter the push, file the deployment handoff. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f."}